course: dictionary
lesson: 14408
title: Too many in one place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Overcrowding is a noun. It means there are too many people or things in one place, so the place is too full. Look at the parts: over means too much, and crowd means a lot of people or things together.
explain: «Overcrowding in the old classroom meant there was no space to sit down.» The clue is no space to sit down: there were too many children for the room. Try your meaning in the sentence: "too many people in one place, so it was too full" fits, so you have it right.
explain: Overcrowding can also mean the act of putting too many people or things into a place. The -ing form of the verb overcrowd is overcrowding, so you may see it as an action too. The word is the same, but the clues in the sentence show which meaning is used.
fact: Overcrowding is a noun that means there are too many people or things in one place.
fact: Overcrowding is also the -ing form of the verb overcrowd, which means to put too many people or things into a place.
fact: «Overcrowding in the city's streets led to a lot of illness.» The sentence shows that too many people in one place caused problems.
fact: In science, overcrowding of plants or animals means they fight for food, water and light.
fact: Phrases you may meet: overcrowding in schools, cause overcrowding, reduce overcrowding.
exercise: «Overcrowding in the old classroom meant there was no space to sit down.» What does overcrowding mean here? | A room painted bright blue | A room with lots of big windows | *Too many children in one room, so it was too full | A very quiet room with no children
exercise: «Too many fish in the pond caused overcrowding, so they fought over the food.» What did the fish fight over? | *Food | Pebbles | Other ponds | Clean boats
exercise: Ali says overcrowding means a quiet, empty place. What does it really mean? | A place for sleeping | A very quiet place | *Too many people or things in one place, so it is too full | A place with plenty of room to spare
test: «Overcrowding at the station can cause a crush.» Why is this a safety problem? | The station is too clean to use | Trains always run on time when it is busy | *People can get squashed when too many are packed into one place
test: Which phrase means to make overcrowding smaller? | Overcrowding in schools | *Reduce overcrowding | Cause overcrowding
exam: Which sentence uses overcrowding correctly? | The beach had so much overcrowding that the sand was empty | Overcrowding was a sunny, quiet afternoon | Overcrowding is a colour we painted the walls | *Overcrowding in the bus meant nobody could find a seat
